<title>ITALY: MOTOR RACING-HILL SPINS OUT OF ITALIAN GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-HILL SPINS OUT OF ITALIAN GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>MONZA, Italy 1996-09-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Briton Damon Hill, driving a Williams-Renault, hit a tyre wall and spun out of Sunday's Italian Grand Prix on lap six.</p>
<p>Hill, who was leading at the time, had started the race with a 13-point lead over team mate Jacques Villeneuve of Canada and had hoped to clinch his first drivers' championship title with a victory at Monza.</p>
